//@ run-pass
//@ expect-stdout: REGALLOC_PRESSURE_STORE_OK
// Register allocation stress test: 187 live f64 values.
//
// BUG: at 187 live values, the Sounio register allocator corrupts
// 94 of 187 values. At 186 values, all pass. This test pins the bug.
//
// Root cause: the spill slot offset calculation in
// native_v2_spill_slot_offset() does not match the IR slot layout
// used by ir_slot_offset(). When values are spilled, the store and
// load use different stack offsets, corrupting the values.
//
// This is the same class of bug as Triton #11111: under register
// pressure, a computation can produce a value that is stored to the
// wrong location.

fn clamp_lo(x: f64, lo: f64) -> f64 {
    if x > lo { x } else { lo }
}

